# Keeps the Dockerfile's `COPY . .` from baking local secrets and state into the image.
# Anything listed here must be either a secret, machine-local state that the /data volume
# owns in production, or not needed at runtime.

# Secrets
# `**/` prefix is load-bearing here for the same reason as the bytecode patterns below, but
# a miss costs more: a bare pattern is anchored to the context root, so a nested `.env` or
# `.pem` would be baked into the image as a live credential rather than merely bloat it.
# `**/` matches zero or more leading segments, so root-level `.env` is still excluded.
**/.env*
.streamlit/secrets.toml
.streamlit/*token*.json
.streamlit/oauth_states.json

# Local state the /data volume owns in production
app.db
app.db-wal
app.db-shm
.cache/

# VCS and build junk
.git/
.gitignore
# `**/` prefix is required: .dockerignore patterns are anchored to the context root, so a
# bare `__pycache__/` would only match one at the root and miss every nested one.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache/
.venv/
node_modules/
.DS_Store

# Local TLS certs
**/*.pem

# Not needed at runtime
tests/
docs/
tickets/
.team/
reference/
scripts/
team-generator/
.devcontainer/
.claude/
.claudeignore
WORKFLOW.md
